WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
My guest tonight is a hilarious comedian

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:06.070
and actress who hosts the
Netflix series Nailed It,

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:08.500
as well as five podcasts.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.290
Good god, five!

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:13.480
Including Why Don't You Date Me.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.880
Her new book is called
#VERYFAT #VERYBRAVE.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.680
Please welcome our good
friend Nicole Byer.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.620
Nicole, we will get to the
book in just a few minutes,

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:26.290
but first of all, tell
me, you look gorgeous.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:27.544
You look beautiful.

00:00:27.544 --> 00:00:28.812
Thank you, Conan.

00:00:28.812 --> 00:00:30.220
Yes, I love the regal.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.900
And how are you doing these days?

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.820
You know, honestly I
think most Black people

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.460
have had a rough couple of weeks.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:46.280
It's been not fun, but also nice to see

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:49.250
so many people feel emboldened

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:50.680
to be in the streets with us,

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.330
to be protesting with us.

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:55.140
That feels good, but
you know it just sucks

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:58.300
that another Black man was
killed that was unarmed,

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.380
and woman!

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:00.680
Breonna Taylor, you know.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:03.080
It's (beep) up.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:04.620
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.150
That's a good summation.

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:08.870
(laughter)

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:11.130
Not quite as eloquent
as some of the speeches

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:14.410
I have heard, but probably
the most to the point.

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:15.243
Oh yeah.

00:01:15.243 --> 00:01:18.732
Would you say that, and I don't want

00:01:18.732 --> 00:01:20.830
to lead you with this question,

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:25.830
but is the reaction making you
more hopeful, less hopeful?

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:29.740
Where do you think you are, personally?

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:32.940
Um, I think the reaction makes me

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:36.780
incredibly hopeful because I feel

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:39.040
like too many people were radicalized

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:43.450
who understand that we have
been going through this shit

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:48.450
for so long, 450 years,
like the longest time!

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:52.100
We got brought over, we
weren't treated very nicely

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.640
because slavery was bad.

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:57.230
And then after slavery,
Jim Crow, that was awful.

00:01:57.230 --> 00:01:59.400
Like, I still have aunts
who are still alive

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:00.680
who remember segregation.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:02.650
Like, that's insane to me.

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:05.610
So I think a lot of white
people's eyes were opened

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:08.720
and that, to me, makes me so excited.

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:11.460
Like, my roommate is a very white man.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.010
Oh, he's so white.

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:16.540
And he was going to protests with me,

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:18.440
and was explaining to his mom

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:21.280
that police brutality is a
real thing and it's awful.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:24.680
And then he went to a protest by himself,

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:27.230
and then I came home and he was humming

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:29.810
a chant from the protest
and frying chicken,

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:34.140
and I was like, did this go
fully in the other direction?

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:36.010
What is going on?

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:38.400
But it's so nice.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.100
You think maybe he went too far,

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.270
or do you think it was still okay?

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:44.790
Oh, it was chicken nuggets.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:47.410
It wasn't like deep fried chicken,

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:50.689
so I was like it's not
super all the way there.

00:02:50.689 --> 00:02:54.290
He's like just teetering
around, but I appreciate it.

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:56.410
I appreciate that he's
going to protests alone.

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:58.340
I appreciate that my white friends

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:00.370
for the most part have
not been bothering me.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:02.120
I got good white people in my life

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:05.370
who are posting for each
other's shit they should read.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:07.320
Nobody's going, Nicole,
what should I read.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.730
What should I be doing?

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:09.990
Like, they've been doing the work.

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:12.510
My one friend Elinor, she sends me stuff.

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:14.280
She'll be like, this protest is happening.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:18.157
And I'm like, this is an
active ally, not a good ally.

00:03:18.157 --> 00:03:19.820
Because we need active allies.

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:21.980
You can be as good as you
want inside your house,

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:24.215
but that's not going to
do anything for anybody.

00:03:24.215 --> 00:03:27.115
Yeah, it's one of the things
that I think about is,

00:03:27.115 --> 00:03:29.870
and I've been talking to
a lot of different people

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:33.110
in the last two weeks
who have been telling me

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:35.580
over and over again that Black people

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:38.298
are tired of explaining their situation.

00:03:38.298 --> 00:03:39.131
Oh yeah!

00:03:39.131 --> 00:03:40.950
That it's exhausting and their saying

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:43.030
you go, you white people go out,

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:45.780
do your homework, you do the work,

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:49.700
and get back to us or
whatever you gotta do,

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:53.140
but please stop asking us to explain

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:55.710
over and over and over again

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:58.280
as if this is a new phenomenon.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:59.380
Yeah, it's not new.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:02.700
It's been around since everybody
on this planet was born.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.727
Also, like Google.com.

00:04:04.727 --> 00:04:06.090
(laughing)

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:08.570
It's filled with so much information.

00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:10.900
And yeah, Black people,
we've been talking about it.

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:14.830
Like, in my stand up shows
I spend about 10 minutes

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:18.430
talking about racial injustices

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:20.320
and being racially profiled.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.900
I mean, it is comedy and it is funny,

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:25.220
and every now and again
at a meet and greet

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:27.650
I'll have someone be like,
did that really happen to you.

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:29.980
And I was like, why
would I lie about that?

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:32.360
It's a horrific experience
that I found the humor in,

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:34.460
because that's what Black
people have been doing

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:36.050
for the longest time.

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:38.500
Awful shit happens to us
and then we turn it around

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:40.270
and we make it fun and funny

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:42.820
because how else would we survive.

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:46.650
Slaves sang songs because
they had to find joy,

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:49.420
even though they were living
this horrible existence.

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:50.510
Right, right.

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:53.252
It is interesting that people think,

00:04:53.252 --> 00:04:56.950
obviously the last two
weeks has been filled.

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:59.200
It started with this horrific image

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:04.200
of George Floyd's killing
and we went from there,

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:06.820
but it is amazing to think

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:09.951
that comedians like yourself

00:05:09.951 --> 00:05:14.750
are able to walk this sort of knife edge

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:18.930
of talking about it, getting
your feelings out about it,

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:22.970
but also miraculously somehow
making it very funny at times

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:26.817
that might speak to people who
might not otherwise hear you.

00:05:26.817 --> 00:05:30.860
It's interesting, it's
amazing what comedy can do.

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:31.980
Yeah, like Chris Rock.

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:33.130
This has been floating around,

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:34.900
I think it was in his last special,

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:37.660
but he was like, cops, a few bad apples,

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:39.210
I'm butchering this man's joke,

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:41.040
but it essentially was just like,

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.300
what if American Airlines was
like we got a few bad apples.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.580
A couple of them like
to crash into mountains.

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:48.650
And it's like, yeah, why do we keep saying

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:51.420
that a few bad apples is
okay in a police department?

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:52.874
That's no!

00:05:52.874 --> 00:05:56.100
I had one bad apple in
a bowl, and guess what?

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:57.880
The rest of the apples tasted like shit.

00:05:57.880 --> 00:05:59.730
So I think that's what's happening.

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:01.197
Right, right.

00:06:01.197 --> 00:06:06.197
You've talked about how racial inequality

00:06:06.927 --> 00:06:09.920
can manifest itself in healthcare,

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:12.380
which is something
probably a lot of people

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:13.490
aren't fully aware of.

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:15.440
They're aware of, we hear about

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:18.170
the more overt, blatant forms

00:06:18.170 --> 00:06:21.803
of racial inequality, but healthcare.

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:25.550
And you've experienced that yourself.

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:26.383
Oh yeah.

00:06:27.294 --> 00:06:30.450
I fully flew off a motorcycle in December.

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:33.430
I was taking my road test and I failed it

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:35.980
in maybe the most spectacular way,

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:39.820
and I was limping and I had
this huge gash in my leg.

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:43.480
And I went to urgent care
and they took an X ray,

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:45.220
and they were like here are some crutches

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:47.440
and here's a great
recommendation of an ice pack.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:48.400
And I was like, that's it?

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:50.390
And they were like, we don't
think you need any more.

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:52.370
And then like two weeks later
I was in Buffalo, New York

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:54.350
with one of my dear friends, Kristy,

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:56.720
and she had a sinus infection

00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:58.910
so she went to urgent care

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:00.990
and then they gave her
like Tylenol codeine,

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:02.820
a Z pack and all this shit.

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:04.730
And I was like, wait what?

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:07.380
And then I started doing literally

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:09.100
the slightest amount of research.

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:11.960
I went to my friend
Google.com and googled this,

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:15.190
and apparently it stems from slavery times

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:17.840
where people were like Black people

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:20.070
heal faster, they're stronger,

00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:22.080
they don't experience pain,

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:23.840
and it was to make
white people feel better

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:28.040
about trading human beings
and whipping human beings

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:32.400
and Black women, specifically,
get the least amount of care.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:35.910
We die sometimes in awful ways.

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:37.180
Like there was a woman,

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:39.140
she was a teacher in Brooklyn, I believe.

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:40.150
She went to the hospital.

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:41.550
She said she had shortness of breath,

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:42.890
she wasn't feeling good.

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:44.840
She thought she had COVID-19.

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:46.030
They sent her home.

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:48.080
She called an ambulance to her house.

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:49.380
They said she was fine.

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:51.030
And then she made her way to the hospital,

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:52.550
was on a ventilator for like two weeks,

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:54.890
and then died because nobody believed her.

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:57.540
And they think that Black people

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:01.240
are like seeking
narcotics or whatever, but

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:05.560
I can't believe you took
the Hippocratic Oath

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:06.950
and you can't look someone in the eye

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:08.420
and just try to help them.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:10.527
Mm-hm.

00:08:10.527 --> 00:08:13.773
You're saying that
there's literally a sense

00:08:13.773 --> 00:08:18.773
that a white physician might have

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:22.630
that this Black person doesn't not feel

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:25.900
the amount of pain that we feel,

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:29.280
so I don't need to give them, prescribe

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:32.910
the really good Tylenol
because they're not feeling

00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:34.870
what my white patient is feeling.

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:36.250
Correct.

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:37.640
Or they just don't believe us.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:41.100
Maybe he thought I was lying
about being on a motorcycle,

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:42.610
but no, I'm trying real hard.

00:08:42.610 --> 00:08:44.660
2020, I'm gonna be a bad ass.

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:46.900
But it's been hard.

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:47.990
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:49.605
Are you really riding a
motorcycle these days?

00:08:49.605 --> 00:08:51.410
Yes!

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:53.090
I bought a motorcycle, but I truly

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:55.130
only take it around my cul-de-sac,

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:56.820
because I was like, if I fall off again

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:58.940
and I actually have to
go to a real hospital,

00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:01.400
COVID-19, I don't want that!

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:04.610
Right, well wear the
helmet for god's sake,

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:07.100
even if you're going 20 yards.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:10.984
Wear the helmet and wear the
good jackets with the armor.

00:09:10.984 --> 00:09:13.577
Mm-hmm, and I have armored pants now.

00:09:13.577 --> 00:09:15.430
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:17.320
None of this riding around in Daisy Dukes.

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:19.253
We'll talk about that later.

00:09:19.253 --> 00:09:20.920
(laughing)

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:23.200
I wanted to congratulate you

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:26.850
because Nailed It, you were nominated

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:29.260
Critics Choice Award for female star.

00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:30.520
That's really exciting.

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:33.230
It is exciting because I am a star

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:35.643
and I'm so glad that
people are taking notice!

00:09:35.643 --> 00:09:36.490
No, I'm kidding.

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:38.197
It's nice.

00:09:38.197 --> 00:09:39.240
But you're not kidding.

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:40.940
People love the show.

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:42.580
You're so funny on the show

00:09:43.477 --> 00:09:45.777
and it's connected you
to this whole audience.

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:48.183
I mean, kids!

00:09:48.183 --> 00:09:49.750
I mean, adults love the show, as well,

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:51.920
but kids go crazy for your show.

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:53.940
They love you, which is nice.

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:57.380
You're speaking directly
to all these young people.

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:58.423
That's fantastic.

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:00.203
Thanks!

00:10:00.203 --> 00:10:02.240
I mean, I don't like kids.

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:04.198
I just, there's something about them.

00:10:04.198 --> 00:10:06.448
(laughter)

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:09.570
They got too many questions.

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:11.980
They're sticky.

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:14.220
A bunch of kids have been
drawing pictures of me

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:16.120
and their parents are
posting it on Twitter,

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:18.286
and I'm like, this is bad!

00:10:18.286 --> 00:10:19.260
(laughter)

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:21.000
Why are you sending this to me?

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.690
Keep this, I don't want this!

00:10:22.690 --> 00:10:24.130
We're already having a bad week.

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:25.869
I don't want to look at
your kid's ugly drawing.

00:10:25.869 --> 00:10:28.770
They're adorable.

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:31.500
You've got this great
critically-acclaimed show.

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:32.880
People love it, it's a hit.

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:34.620
It's got a huge kid fan base,

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:37.076
and you're going after kids, okay.

00:10:37.076 --> 00:10:38.820
(laughter)

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:40.370
Only you would do that.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:42.020
I want to talk about your book.

00:10:42.020 --> 00:10:43.077
Congratulations.

00:10:43.077 --> 00:10:47.870
#VERYFAT #VERYBRAVE and it is filled

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:50.331
with amazing photographs.

00:10:50.331 --> 00:10:51.331
Thank you.

00:10:52.453 --> 00:10:53.860
Really fantastic photographs.

00:10:53.860 --> 00:10:57.130
Your photographer, your
poses are incredible.

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:58.545
Conan, thank you.

00:10:58.545 --> 00:11:02.030
I love, there's a picture in
here I ant find it right now

00:11:02.030 --> 00:11:04.370
of you in front of an In-N-Out.

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:05.610
Oh yeah.

00:11:05.610 --> 00:11:07.683
I love this picture.

00:11:07.683 --> 00:11:09.640
[Nicole] Thank you!

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:12.794
Just, I mean, we've all been there.

00:11:12.794 --> 00:11:13.810
(laughter)

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:17.190
I've been in front of an In-N-Out
in my leopard skin bikini

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:19.350
and this is really a great.

00:11:19.350 --> 00:11:20.270
What is your message?

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:23.820
What is your message
with #VERYFAT #VERYBRAVE,

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:27.010
because the photographs
alone are terrific,

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:28.660
but I know that you're trying

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:30.400
to accomplish a little more here.

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:31.233
A little bit.

00:11:31.233 --> 00:11:32.930
My friend Kim Newmoney took the pictures

00:11:32.930 --> 00:11:35.120
and my friend Allison Rich was like,

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:36.490
you should do a coffee table book.

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:38.200
And I was like, okay.

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:39.240
And then as I was writing it,

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:41.300
I was like, it's so dumb that people call

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:44.070
fat women brave for wearing bikinis.

00:11:44.070 --> 00:11:46.110
So I was like, why don't I just make fun

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:48.860
of that whole weird phenomenon.

00:11:48.860 --> 00:11:50.390
But I hope people read the book.

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:51.911
I mean, it's a quick read.

00:11:51.911 --> 00:11:54.770
Truly you can read it
in like an hour or two,

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:57.050
but I hope people finish it

00:11:57.050 --> 00:12:00.400
and then go, why did I ever give a shit

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:02.050
about what people think about me?

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:03.810
Why did I ever care?

00:12:03.810 --> 00:12:05.620
If someone stares at me,

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:09.000
that means my body
disrupted their life enough

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:11.320
that they needed to stop what
they were doing to look at me,

00:12:11.320 --> 00:12:13.600
that means my body is powerful.

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:17.600
Also, every body is
beautiful in its own way.

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:19.050
And every body is different.

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:22.360
And the world is all right
like really, really hard,

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:25.260
so why would you spend it hating
what you see in the mirror?

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:28.520
That's like an extra layer of misery.

00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:31.303
Have you, you've always been,

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:33.807
and I think it's a
remarkable quality you have,

00:12:33.807 --> 00:12:37.060
but you're just always so
comfortable with yourself.

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:40.010
And I'm curious is that
who you've always been,

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:42.143
or did you have to get to that place?

00:12:43.290 --> 00:12:46.010
I've always been pretty
comfortable with myself.

00:12:46.010 --> 00:12:48.832
My mom used to call me
Tina because I would scream

00:12:48.832 --> 00:12:52.710
a lot like Tina Turner and
I listed to Tina Turner

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:53.870
and scream along to that.

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:57.390
And I've always kinda marched
to my own little drumbeat.

00:12:57.390 --> 00:12:58.223
I don't know.

00:12:58.223 --> 00:13:01.910
It's more fun to just
figure out who you are

00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:03.172
and just be that.

00:13:03.172 --> 00:13:05.780
Spending time trying to be somebody else

00:13:05.780 --> 00:13:09.686
seems so exhausting and also crazy.

00:13:09.686 --> 00:13:11.063
Yeah, yeah.

00:13:13.144 --> 00:13:16.370
I grew up not liking
anything about myself.

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:17.864
Well, why?

00:13:17.864 --> 00:13:18.697
Conan, you're tall!

00:13:18.697 --> 00:13:20.480
That's luxurious.

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:21.440
You have red hair.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:22.670
How exotic!

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:23.840
You have all your teeth.

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:24.673
What a treat!

00:13:25.514 --> 00:13:27.530
(laughter)

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:29.570
Wait, okay, so you had three qualities

00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:31.580
you liked about me and one of them

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:33.295
was I have all my teeth.

00:13:33.295 --> 00:13:35.545
(laughter)

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:40.390
That did nothing to make me feel better.

00:13:40.390 --> 00:13:43.290
I want to ask you about,
you're on a mission

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:45.690
to get people to embrace spandex.

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:47.460
Let's talk about that.

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:48.960
Why spandex?

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:52.580
Because spandex is your friend.

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:53.920
Like, if you hold something up

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:56.500
and you're like I don't
know if this is gonna fit,

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:57.333
pull it!

00:13:57.333 --> 00:14:00.690
If it has spandex, it probably does fit!

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:04.230
Also, if it's too tight, who cares!

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:05.950
People already know you're fat.

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:08.210
If you wear bigger clothes people will go

00:14:08.210 --> 00:14:09.350
look at that fatty.

00:14:09.350 --> 00:14:11.010
If you wear tighter clothes people will go

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:12.000
look at that fatty.

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:13.173
What's the difference?

00:14:14.146 --> 00:14:14.979
(laughter)

00:14:14.979 --> 00:14:16.594
Who cares!

00:14:16.594 --> 00:14:18.317
Just wear what you want.

00:14:18.317 --> 00:14:19.790
So you think everyone
should be wearing spandex?

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:20.810
Yes, Conan.

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:23.133
I would like you to
wear some spandex, okay?

00:14:24.569 --> 00:14:26.850
No, it's not gonna be good,
it's not gonna be good.

00:14:26.850 --> 00:14:29.010
Come on, Conan, put on some spandex!

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:31.413
Uh, okay.

00:14:33.400 --> 00:14:37.110
Nicole, your logic is just too powerful.

00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:39.090
I say no, and you say yes,

00:14:39.090 --> 00:14:40.723
and so I'm going to do it.

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:43.200
Not happy with my body

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:47.860
and spandex is gonna
bum a lot of people out.

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:50.440
But it might make three people happy.

00:14:50.440 --> 00:14:52.720
That's more than no people.

00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:54.113
(laughter)

00:14:54.113 --> 00:14:55.840
You know what it would
do, it would get laughs,

00:14:55.840 --> 00:14:57.993
which in our profession.

00:14:58.910 --> 00:14:59.830
That's gold.

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:03.543
We love laughs because we're
sad people on the inside.

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:05.860
I don't think you are.

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:07.387
I don't think you're a sad person.

00:15:07.387 --> 00:15:08.837
No I'm not, I'm very happy.

00:15:10.540 --> 00:15:12.050
You have to check out this book.

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:17.050
It's a great read and also
the pictures are fantastic.

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:18.560
It's by Nicole.

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:23.560
It's #VERYFAT #VERYBRAVE
and a terrific book.

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:26.650
Also, Nicole, you have a list

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:29.572
of Black-owned bookstores, is that right,

00:15:29.572 --> 00:15:30.430
that we want to put up?

00:15:30.430 --> 00:15:33.740
Yeah, because it might be
hard after the pandemic

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:35.900
for Black-owned businesses to come back,

00:15:35.900 --> 00:15:37.320
especially since it's harder for us

00:15:37.320 --> 00:15:39.150
to get loans and whatnot.

00:15:39.150 --> 00:15:42.319
So now is the time to support.

00:15:42.319 --> 00:15:44.500
I also have a list of
Black-owned restaurants,

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:47.160
but I think it's only
in LA, in my bio, too.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:48.420
Okay, all right.

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:50.200
Well, like I say, one of the things

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:52.840
that I've been picking up
just in the last two weeks

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:56.020
of conversations is it's not about

00:15:57.490 --> 00:16:01.570
good, I did three things
and now racism is gone.

00:16:01.570 --> 00:16:03.060
We all know that's not gonna happen.

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:06.700
It's about living life
being a little more present,

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:09.900
being a little more
aware and doing the work

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:11.630
every day in small ways.

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:13.550
Sometimes big ways, sometimes small ways

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:16.390
and supporting Black-owned
businesses is huge.

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:17.510
It's a huge thing.

00:16:17.510 --> 00:16:20.130
If you find a Black-owned
coffee shop in your neighborhood

00:16:20.130 --> 00:16:21.870
go there instead of Starbucks.

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:22.870
It's not that hard.

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:26.250
It's just minor adjustments
that you can make in your life

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:28.690
that will deeply impact
someone else's life

00:16:28.690 --> 00:16:30.640
because that Black-owned business

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:34.920
can start generational
wealth to give to their kids,

00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:36.870
which is a beautiful thing.

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:38.440
Yeah, they're also not gonna be

00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:41.870
selling you a Kenny G CD there.

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:44.963
No, you might get
something more interesting.

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:49.560
But I gotta say, Kenny G,
he got good hair, right?

00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:51.260
He got the long hair with the saxophone?

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:52.210
Long hair, yeah, yeah.

00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:53.043
And he's fine.

00:16:53.043 --> 00:16:55.220
I've got no beef with
him, I'm just saying.

00:16:55.220 --> 00:16:58.220
Do you, Conan, do you
have beef with Kenny G?

00:16:58.220 --> 00:17:00.492
Yes I do, he took my woman!

00:17:00.492 --> 00:17:01.325
Oh no!

00:17:02.795 --> 00:17:05.768
I made that up, but it could happen.

00:17:05.768 --> 00:17:08.814
My wife could run off with
Kenny G, it could happen.

00:17:08.814 --> 00:17:09.780
I don't think so.

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:11.699
It is so nice to see you.

00:17:11.699 --> 00:17:14.274
Wait, is that Abraham Lincoln behind you?

00:17:14.274 --> 00:17:19.274
This, I've had an Abraham
Lincoln up here forever.

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:22.783
Yeah, it's the last
photograph ever taken of him.

00:17:24.860 --> 00:17:28.617
It's a rare outdoor
photograph of Abraham Lincoln.

00:17:28.617 --> 00:17:30.140
Where he don't have no body.

00:17:30.140 --> 00:17:31.317
What's that?

00:17:31.317 --> 00:17:32.530
He doesn't have a body.

00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:34.430
He had a body, they just didn't have

00:17:35.370 --> 00:17:37.520
an iPhone back then
that caught everything.

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:42.420
So whatever, you know.

00:17:42.420 --> 00:17:44.760
I've got this place.

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:46.130
Conan, how are you?

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:48.700
Has anyone asked how you're doing?

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:50.410
No, it hasn't really occurred to anybody

00:17:50.410 --> 00:17:52.007
to ask me how I'm doing.

00:17:52.007 --> 00:17:53.964
How are you, Conan?

00:17:53.964 --> 00:17:54.797
(laughter)

00:17:54.797 --> 00:17:56.420
Well, I think the last two weeks

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:58.174
has been hardest on me.

00:17:58.174 --> 00:18:00.424
(laughter)

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:04.370
And I'm shocked you're the
first person to notice it!

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:05.810
You're the first person to reach out,

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:09.344
but that's how egotistical I am.

00:18:09.344 --> 00:18:13.163
I somehow thought Black Lives
Matter was all about me.

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:17.977
I got confused, that's what an idiot I am.

00:18:17.977 --> 00:18:21.340
And you're an ally who's learning.

00:18:21.340 --> 00:18:24.150
Well, we all need to learn faster and more

00:18:24.150 --> 00:18:26.010
and more and faster.

00:18:26.010 --> 00:18:28.670
But you know, I'm doing great.

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:30.940
And you know what, I'm very lucky because

00:18:32.125 --> 00:18:35.340
I'm very fortunate that I'm able

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:38.170
to keep doing this thing that I do

00:18:38.170 --> 00:18:41.270
during this time of
COVID and all this unrest

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:44.330
and mostly because it gives
me a lot of hope and joy.

00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:46.940
Like talking to you
today, this is not a job.

00:18:46.940 --> 00:18:49.810
Touching base with you
just makes me happy.

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:51.190
You just bring me a lot of joy

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:52.950
every time you come on the show.

00:18:52.950 --> 00:18:54.630
You're so naturally funny

00:18:54.630 --> 00:18:56.382
and you're such a beautiful spirit

00:18:56.382 --> 00:18:59.480
that seeing you today makes me happy.

00:18:59.480 --> 00:19:00.940
It just really makes me happy.

00:19:00.940 --> 00:19:03.632
Conan, thank you!

00:19:03.632 --> 00:19:05.190
You're saving me right now,

00:19:05.190 --> 00:19:07.299
which is really what it's all about.

00:19:07.299 --> 00:19:09.870
I love how this was a nice compliment

00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:11.959
that went right back to Conan.

00:19:11.959 --> 00:19:14.168
I'm a genius at that.

00:19:14.168 --> 00:19:15.840
(laughter)

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:16.980
Let me hold this up again because I want

00:19:16.980 --> 00:19:19.230
to make sure people check it out.

00:19:19.230 --> 00:19:20.063
#VERYFAT #VERYBRAVE.

00:19:21.020 --> 00:19:21.870
Get this book.

00:19:21.870 --> 00:19:25.360
And Nicole, thank you
so much for being here

00:19:25.360 --> 00:19:28.986
and be well and I can't
wait to see you in person.

00:19:28.986 --> 00:19:29.819
Samesies!

00:19:29.819 --> 00:19:31.884
Conan, I adore you.

00:19:31.884 --> 00:19:33.760
What's that mean, Conan?

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:35.931
You and I have a chemistry.

00:19:35.931 --> 00:19:36.764
What does that mean?

00:19:36.764 --> 00:19:39.070
It just means it's undeniable.

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:41.260
You've been around me and I get around you

00:19:41.260 --> 00:19:43.100
and you know what I'm saying.

00:19:43.100 --> 00:19:45.957
Yeah, I can't wait to
see you again, Conan.

00:19:45.957 --> 00:19:48.059
(laughter)

00:19:48.059 --> 00:19:49.621
Truly, you're delightful.

00:19:49.621 --> 00:19:53.119
Take care, I love you,
and I'll see you soon.

00:19:53.119 --> 00:19:54.893
Bye, Conan!

